<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		Sign in with Apple capability. Required for the
		`sign_in_with_apple` Flutter package (and for App Store
		Review rule 4.8 — if we offer Google or any other third-
		party SSO, we MUST also offer Sign In with Apple on iOS).

		The matching capability must be enabled on the Apple
		Developer App ID `co.pettrack.pettrackApp` (Identifiers →
		App ID → Edit → Sign In with Apple). If this entitlement
		is here but the App ID doesn't have the capability, signing
		fails with "An error occurred while signing in with Apple
		(authorization code couldn't be retrieved)".
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
	<!--
		Access WiFi Information capability.

		THIS is the right entitlement for reading the
		currently-connected WiFi's SSID + BSSID via
		`CNCopyCurrentNetworkInfo` (what network_info_plus calls
		under the hood). Easy to confuse with HotspotConfiguration
		below; the rule is:

		- wifi-info → READ current network info
		- HotspotConfiguration → ADD a network to known networks

		2026-05-11: initial pass only added HotspotConfiguration,
		which signed fine but returned null for SSID + BSSID at
		runtime. The fix was adding this entitlement here.

		Used by the phone-side home-zone setup flow
		(docs/plans/2026-05-11-phone-side-home-zone.md): during
		onboarding the app reads the user's home BSSID + phone GPS
		and sends them to the backend instead of asking the MT710
		to scan from indoors (where its scan fails — 3+ failures
		in device_desired_state for the test IMEI).

		iOS gates this read behind THREE conditions:
		  1. This entitlement.
		  2. NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription granted AND
		     "Precise Location" toggle ON.
		  3. App in foreground when reading.

		If this entitlement is here but the App ID doesn't have
		the matching capability enabled (Apple Developer Portal →
		Identifiers → App ID → Edit → Access WiFi Information),
		signing fails. Automatic signing usually handles this if
		you're logged into Xcode with the right team.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.networking.wifi-info</key>
	<true/>

	<!--
		Hotspot Configuration capability — kept around because
		the v1.5 home-setup flow may want to *offer* to add the
		user's home network as a known network on their phone
		(quality-of-life: app reads BSSID for the home zone AND
		registers the network so iOS rejoins it automatically).
		Not strictly required for Phase A/B of the phone-side
		home-zone plan. Remove if it complicates signing.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.networking.HotspotConfiguration</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
